==English==

===Etymology===
{{prefix|mono|cotyledon|lang=en}}

===Pronunciation===
{{rfp|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|botany|lang=en}} Any plant whose seedlings typically have one [[cotyledon]] ([[seed leaf]]) (in contrast to the two cotyledons typical of [[dicot]]s), thereby belonging to the taxonomic [[monocots]], formerly variously known as ''{{taxlink|Monocotyledones|class|noshow=1}}'', ''{{taxlink|Monocotyledonae|class|noshow=1}}'', or [[Liliopsida]], a class in the [[Angiospermae]], the [[flowering plant]]s. This group include the [[grass]]es, [[lilies]], [[orchid]]s and [[palm]]s.

====Usage notes====
* Outside definitions or strict taxonomic usage, {{term|monocot}} is the preferred form.

====Synonyms====
* [[monocot]]
* [[liliopsid]]

====See also====
* [[dicotyledon]]

